A||||3||DaveL||Exhausted Manifold Compatibility  New? Used?||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||06-20-2001||03:33 PM||||I am about to buy a manifold for my 87 2.5, and a friend tells me he has one from some other 87 chevy with a 2.5, and thinks it's the same. I doubt it, maybe the end that goes against the engine is the same, but the flange end has to be different. Are exhaust manifolds from any other vehicle usable?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steven||06-20-2001||03:54 PM||||The 87 Fiero w/ 2.5 liter motor used a 10044374. That manifold was used on GM's A & N cars. A cars are the Celebrity/6000 and the N car is the Grand Am/ Olds. Calais/Buick Somerset-Skylark. Now I am not saying "no other manifolds will work." What I am say is that GM say for the 87 model year these vehicles used the same part as the Fiero.<p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||06-20-2001||06:07 PM||||It might work.  The manifold on my blazer looked identical.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||06-20-2001||08:30 PM||||That I've seen... And I've seen a bunch... All 87 & up FWD GM product with the 2.5l motor uses the same manifold. I've used them from both Olds Cutlass Calais and Grand Am. <P>With minor diferances the whole power train is the same. Minor,,, like the shifting cables/brackets, engine mounts, belt driven stuff. ||||reg||1
